{%- comment -%}
  Industries & applications — port of storefront/src/pages/IndustryPages.jsx and
  data/industries.js, whose own header says the content was "supplied verbatim
  by the store".

  ONE page carries all eight. React had an index plus eight detail routes; that
  would need nine Shopify pages, and pages can only be created through the Admin
  API, which the Theme Access token this theme deploys with cannot reach. So
  each industry is an <details> panel that opens in place: same content, same
  headings, one page to create.

  Product links resolve through all_products at render time, so a renamed or
  unpublished product degrades to the catalogue rather than a dead link.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Handle gate — see snippets/hnl-page for the full explanation: pages on this
  store all render through templates/page.json, so each section declares which
  handle it belongs to.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign hnl_gate = section.settings.page_handle | strip -%}
{%- if hnl_gate == blank or hnl_gate == page.handle -%}
<main id="main" class="page">
